 :closure-fixes
 [{:fix "snapshot limits are exact"
   :was "the entry and byte checks ran at the top of the next iteration, so a terminal entry could put the manifest one entry or one whole file past the stated maximum"
   :now "checked before the entry is added; the refusal names the entry that crossed the line; tests pin the boundary from both sides"}
  {:fix "absolute symlinks are refused"
   :was "a link was refused only when its target lay outside the project root, so an absolute link under the root was accepted"
   :now "every absolute target is refused; relative targets that stay under the root are not"
   :why "a fidelity question, not a containment question: an absolute link cannot escape, because the worker resolves it inside its own filesystem, but /host/project/lib/foo is not /work/lib/foo, so the manifest would describe a tree that was not handed over"}]

 :defects-found
 ["killing the machine manager orphans the machine, which keeps running and consuming CPU; the process primitive now reaps descendants first"
  "the overlay lower layer is the live host tree, so a concurrent host write is visible to the workload and can produce a torn read; a run whose project moved reports no input coordinate"
  "an unhinted .size on BasicFileAttributes resolved reflectively, passing every JVM test and failing in the native image on the first native gate run"
  "the machine manager writes a progress banner to stderr and has no quiet flag, so it was being reported as workload output; it is removed and its bytes removed from the count"
  "overlayfs refuses an overlayfs upperdir, which the machine's own root is; the upper lives on the machine's ext4 disk"]

 :nonclaims
 ["Linux x86_64 with KVM only; no claim about macOS, Windows, aarch64, or a host without /dev/kvm"
  "the dogfood is a babashka project check, not bbagent's own JVM suite; running that would need a JDK and ~/.m2 mounted read-only, which was not done"
  "CPU is configured, not independently bounded: a machine gets a vCPU count, not a share or quota"
  "process count inside a machine is not bounded or measured"
  "the input coordinate detects that a project moved under a run; it does not prevent the workload from having seen the move, and it is not a transaction"
  "isolation rests on the hypervisor and on the read-only mount; no claim about a malicious guest kernel, container equivalence, or multi-tenant security"
  "truncating a stream at a byte budget can split a UTF-8 sequence, so kept text may end in a replacement character; the reported byte count is unaffected"
  "no claim about package installation, long-running services, or background processes; A3a runs one command to completion or to its deadline"
  "the image digest is an artifact identifier, not a reproducibility claim"]

